        "step_title": "SynoCli Kernel Tools",
        "items": [
            {
                "desc": "<b>Experimental, at your own risk.</b> The kernel modules of SynoCommunity packages are outside of what Synology supports: a module that does not suit the kernel can crash the NAS, and DSM updates may break them. Support is limited: read the documentation, and check the issues already open, before opening one. Do not use them on a NAS you cannot afford to restart or recover."
            },
            {
                "desc": "<b>synocli-kernelmodule</b> loads the kernel modules of the <b>synokernel-*</b> packages, one device at a time, through its profile; it holds the profiles of every such package. It does not load anything by itself, on installation nor at boot. Run it with <b>sudo -i</b> in front: sudo alone does not find the commands of packages.<br><br><code>synocli-kernelmodule list</code><br><code>sudo -i synocli-kernelmodule --profile cdrom start</code><br><br>See the <a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://docs.synocommunity.com/packages/synocli-kernel/\">package documentation</a>, and <a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://docs.synocommunity.com/packages/synocli-kernel/#loading-modules-at-boot\">Loading modules at boot</a> for the scheduled task that loads them at every startup."
            }
        ]
    }
